'[Mission Dialog]'

'[Triggered Text]'

'[Info]'
Title = "Gasoline Alley";
briefing = "Gasoline Alley
Date: August 27, 2003 - 2015 hours 
Location:  Mogadishu Outskirts, Somalia

Situation:
We have our first mission for Task Force Ranger today. Aidid's financial chief, Osman Otto, operates a warehouse where they are outfitting trucks with fifty-caliber machine guns. We need to capture those technicals and destroy them.";
briefing2 = "<cFC8932>Gasoline Alley<-co>
OPORD: 1-93 TFR  Date Time: 272015 August 93  

1. <ucFC8932>Situation<-uco>
 Aidid's financial chief, Osman Otto, operates a warehouse in Mog. where they are outfitting pickup trucks with .50 caliber machine guns that pose a threat to UNOSOM II forces.
      <cFC8932>Weather:<-co>  High clouds, low light.
      <cFC8932>Terrain:<-co> Urban.
      <cFC8932>Enemy:<-co>  Intel places guards at the perimeters and along your ingress, but no fortified positions. Strong Habr Gedir presence, possibility of reinforcements from neighboring area. Guard and possible roadblocks protect access routes.
      <cFC8932>Friendly:<-co>  None

2. <ucFC8932>Mission<-uco> 
      <cFC8932>Who:<-co> Ranger Platoons 2 and 3
      <cFC8932>What:<-co> Insert by Humvee, locate garage and destroy technicals inside.      <cFC8932>When:<-co> 2015 hours (dusk) depart Task Force Ranger base at Mogadishu Airport.

3. <ucFC8932>Execution<-uco>
Commander's Intent: Secure and destroy technicals. All forces return to base.
      <cFC8932>Concept of Operation:<-co>  Two teams of Rangers will infil and make the final assault on foot along route red. Teams will get as deep into enemy territory as possible before enemy can raise an alarm. 
      <cFC8932>Coordinating instructions:<-co>  Platoon 4 will extract all personnel once action on the objective is complete.

4. <ucFC8932>Service and Support<-uco>
      <cFC8932>Basic Load:<-co>  M16, M9 Beretta, Satchel Charges, Night Vision Goggles

5. <ucFC8932>Command and signal<-uco>
Command Post (CP) Black will coordinate assault from TFR base. Task Force chain of command in effect. Hand and arm signals TACSOP, with higher via FM primary and SATCOM alternate.  Standard unit CEOI

";

'[WinConditions]'
